   mirroring the players line's three constraints (states the mechanic, echoes the block's name,
   avoids "leader", names no metric) but keeping "Season to date" rather than "Season totals to
   date" — the team boards are per-match rates, not sums.
+
+2026-08-19 fix/team-name-overrides-pool1-remainder — team_name_overrides batch 2: Bundesliga,
+Eredivisie, Ligue 1, Liga Portugal. 36 more corrections, one standing exclusion caught before it
+shipped wrong.
+
+  ⚠ SELF-CONTAINED BY DESIGN. This entry repeats the full ruling rather than pointing at the
+  sibling branch's own entry (fix/team-name-overrides-pool1, MR !77), because that branch has not
+  merged to main — a reviewer working from this branch alone cannot see it. Round-1 review FAILed
+  the previous version of this task for citing that entry as if it were reachable here. It is not,
+  until !77 merges.
+
+  THE RULING, IN FULL, as given in chat: CPO objected to "Inter" and "Arsenal" as example browse
+  chips, then: "The name is Arsenal London and not Arsenal England. We have to fix and standardize
+  these names." Corrected further: "however, it's not Arsenal London. It's Arsenal FC. But it's
+  Inter Milan... So whatever, if we can't rely on what the provider gives us, we have to define the
+  name we use as the single source of truth for what we display." That is the authority for
+  broadening `team_name_overrides` from collision-only to also cover unique-but-incomplete names,
+  used first on branch fix/team-name-overrides-pool1 (61 rows, PL/PD/SA) and continued here.
+
+  Continuation of that same-day ruling. Same method: fetch each league's current club list, verify
+  against English Wikipedia, add only what's confidently sourced.
+
+  ⚠ CAUGHT BEFORE SHIPPING: Bayern München (team_api_id 157) was NOT corrected to "FC Bayern
+  Munich" despite that being English Wikipedia's actual article title, because the seed's own
+  standing rule (dbt_project/seeds/schema.yml) already excludes exactly this: "Bayern München is
+  NOT corrected to Bayern Munich (CPO ruled one locale-independent slug)." München vs Munich is a
+  LOCALE preference, not a completeness defect — mechanically applying "match Wikipedia's title"
+  without checking for this would have reintroduced a rule this project already reversed once.
+  Worth recording because the broadened trigger (this session) and the older locale exclusion
+  (pre-existing) could easily be conflated by a future pass that doesn't re-read the standing rule
+  first.
+
+  ~15 teams across the four leagues were NOT corrected, left unchanged rather than guessed: the
+  Wikipedia source's current-season club table didn't clearly cover them (likely promoted/relegated
+  since the article was last edited, or the summary was ambiguous). BL1: 1. FC Heidenheim, FC St.
+  Pauli, VfL Wolfsburg. ED: ADO Den Haag, Cambuur, Excelsior, FC Volendam, Telstar, Willem II
+  (contradictory summary). L1: Estac Troyes, Le Mans, RED Star FC 93, Rodez, Saint Etienne. LP:
+  Academico Viseu, Maritimo, Torreense, AVS (summary looked implausible, not trusted without a
+  second check).
+
+  WHAT SHIPPED: 36 rows, each cited to an English Wikipedia URL. (Corrected from an initial "35" —
+  a plain arithmetic error, L1 was 13 rows not 12, caught by analytics-engineer-reviewer round 1.)
+
+  Pool 1 status after this batch: PL/PD/SA done (61, MR !77) + BL1/ED/L1/LP done (36, this branch)
+  = 97 corrections total, plus the ~15 above and 2 confirmed-no-change (Athletic Club, Real Madrid)
+  and Feyenoord (confirmed already correct) still open or resolved-as-no-change. Beyond Pool 1 is
+  not started.
+
+
+2026-08-19 fix/team-name-overrides-pool1 — team_name_overrides extended past collision-only:
+provider "crap names" (CPO's word) are systemic, not isolated to one or two clubs.
+
+  HOW IT SURFACED. Designing a sitewide browse-chip feature (random sample from an active
+  team/player/competition pool), "Inter" and "Arsenal" showed up as example chips. CPO asked
+  whether these are actually single-source display names, then: "we don't use Inter as the display
+  name for Inter Milan... It's Arsenal FC and not Arsenal."
+
+  THE EXISTING MECHANISM WAS TOO NARROW. `team_name_overrides` (9 rows, #850/#851) only fires on a
+  COLLISION — two real clubs sharing the byte-identical provider string. Checked: neither Arsenal
+  nor Inter collides with anything ("Arsenal", "Arsenal Tula", "Arsenal Sarandi" are already
+  different strings), so the existing trigger would never have caught either one.
+
+  RULING — THE BAR IS COMPLETENESS, NOT JUST UNIQUENESS. CPO: "we have to define the name we use
+  as the single source of truth for what we display." A provider name can be unique in our data
+  and still not be the club's real display name.
+
+  SCALE, MEASURED NOT GUESSED. First sample was 9 clubs pulled while investigating the browse-chip
+  question, spread across PL/SA/PD/ED/L1 (mislabeled "Bundesliga's 21" in an earlier draft of this
+  entry — WRONG, corrected here; none of the 9 were BL1). 8 of 9 needed correction (Arsenal, Inter,
+  Barcelona, Ajax, Monaco, Lyon, Marseille, Malaga); one, Feyenoord, was already correct despite
+  LOOKING short — so "looks incomplete" is not by itself a reliable signal, every name needs an
+  actual check, not a pattern match.
+
+  Second pass covered the REST of PL, PD and SA properly (fetched each league's full current-club
+  list against Wikipedia). Result: 53 more corrections out of roughly 58 teams checked across the
+  three leagues — i.e. the overwhelming majority of two of the biggest leagues in the pool were
+  sending an incomplete provider name. Two flagged UNCERTAIN rather than guessed: "Athletic Club"
+  (the club's own preferred name may already be correct, "Athletic Bilbao" is the more common
+  foreign-press form — not corrected pending a closer check) and "Real Madrid" (arguably already
+  unambiguous without a suffix, unlike Barcelona/Monaco/Lyon — held pending a call rather than
+  applying the mechanical "match Wikipedia's title" rule without judgment).
+
+  Still unchecked: BL1, ED, L1, LP (roughly 80 more teams), and everything outside Pool 1 if the
+  browse pool ever extends there.
+
+  WHAT SHIPPED THIS ROUND: 61 rows added to `team_name_overrides.csv` total (8 from the mixed
+  sample + 53 from PL/PD/SA), each cited to its English Wikipedia article URL, same format as the
+  existing 9.
+
+  NOT DECIDED: how far the sweep extends beyond what has been checked so far, and a call on the
+  two flagged-uncertain rows. Being decided iteratively in chat, not pre-committed.
